            BRIEF DESCRIPTIONS OF FILES IN OPLEXAMP.ZIP
                                 
                  Mike Niklaus :  7th March, 1995
                                 
Because I didn't have the time to download and try out each
program, I simply read the .txt and .opl files and attempted to
work out what any code in them did.  I am new to the Psion S3 and
S3a so please forgive the queries and probable inaccuracies in the
following list.

It will be much appreciated by me if any expert reading this
document is able to let Steve Lichfield have an updated version of
it.

                                 #
3aeval.opl      Uses  OOPS methods to allow  a  graphics  prog  to
perform evaluation?

                                 A
Aalam.opl      Details of calls to OS time.
Abstim.opl      Demonstrates how to set up a  timer  using  system
time  and  launch  an   application when  the  timer  duration  is
completed.
Agendfmt.txt   Details of how agenda files are formatted.
Alarms.opl     Alarm setting program.
Alarm.opl      Alarm setting program.
And.opl         Complex  text about overflows and  using  the  AND
operator.
Assemb.opl      Assembler prog snippet regarding  two  dimensional
arrays(?)
Atten.opl      Calculates electrical impedances.
Attime.txt      Shoes how to make Psion switch on at  a  specified
time.
Attrib.opl      Shows  how to set file attributes  from  within  a
prog.
Attrib.opo     Presumably the run time module of Attrib.opl(?)

                                 B
Basechng.opl   Prog which converts values from one numeric base to
another.
Batchchk.opl   Displays battery voltages.
Battery.opl    Displays Psion battery voltages.
Beeper.opl     Tiny prog which beeps whenever PEEKW ($28) is  non-
zero(!)
Bitmap.opl      Appears  to move an icon around  the  screen  when
various keys are pressed(?)

                                 C
Capture.txt     Runs  specified program  when  specified  keypress
combination detected.
Checkdir.txt    How  to  write  code  to  distinguish  between   a
directory and a file.
Circlex.opl    A quick way of drawing a circle.
Clockcrd.opl   Processes clock card data.
Combsort.opl   Example of a 'comb' sort, used on an array here but
modifiable for .dbf files.
Commtime.txt   How to get your prog to communicate over the serial
link.
Contrast.txt   Prog to read and/or change contrast value.
Conv.opl       Adds conversions to Psion Calculator.
Countdwn.opl   Simple prog to beep after a specified duration.
Cpress.opl     Compresses data files from within your prog.
Ctrlbeep.opl    Demo of a beep prog running at same time  as  chrs
being typed.
Ctrlhelp.opl     Demo  of  Help  file  implementation.    Requires
Dohelp.opo. See below.

                                 D
Datadate.txt   How to extract last update date from a  data  file.
OPL example
Datetrix.txt   Using Integers in dialogs.  Converting  dDATE back
to day,month,year..
Devlist.opl     Prog  to display list of devices  present  on  the
Psion.
Devtype.opl     Prog to display device type on a specified  drive.
(e.g. on A, B).
Divline.txt     How to set/unset dialog dividing lines  where  not
normally possible.
Dohelp.opl       Prog  implements  a  help  facility.    Runs   in
background.
Doubleb.txt    How to improve screen drawing speed.
                Also  warning that only one sprite at  a  time  is
supported.
Dtmf.opl        Method  of  sounding dialling  tones  from  an  S3
program.
                                 E
E12R.opl        Appears  to convert something  using  a  table  of
values, but what?
Encrypt.opl     Demo  of encrypting/decrypting text  ,  using  the
password as a mask.
Export.opl      Writes  .dbf file to a text  file  using  selected
delimiter.
Expow.opl       Sets  Autopower off (&  on?)  using  a  background
program.

  The Ex_*.opl files below come from the Psion S3a progam manual
Ex_alarm.opl   Sets a specified alarm time.
Ex_anima.opl    Animates rectangles of the screen divided  into  5
areas.
Ex_app0.opl    Example of setting up an OPA type 0 application.
Ex_app3.opl    Example of setting up a type 3 OPA application.
Ex_birth.opl   Prog to calculate day of week from specified date
Ex_bounce.opl  Bounces a "0"  around the screen.
Ex_circl.opl   Draws a hollow elipse of specified centre,  radius,
circularity w/o trig.
Ex_circ2.opl   Draws a filled elipse of specified centre,  radius,
circularity w/o trig.
Ex_dice.opl    Prints a random integer in the range 1-6.
Ex_dtmf.opl    Prog to sound DTMF tones.  Uses OS calls.
Ex_eval.opl    Prog demonstrating use of the EVAL command.
Ex_icon.opl    Demo of creating  simple icon.
Ex-ioscr.opl   Demo of I/O calls to set font, size, style etc  for
a selected window.
Ex_iotyp.opl   Returns the type name of a specified file.
Ex_label.opl   Processes a data file to adjust it when you add  an
extra field.
Ex_menus.opl   Demo of using menu commands.
Ex_music.opl    Demo  using  beep  to  sound  notes  of   specific
frequencies.
Ex_reord.opl   Sorts a data file into rising alpha order based  on
contents of 1st field
                Uses Update to move records rather than create  an
index so don't use this  for a file held on a FLASH disk.
Ex_timer.opl   Countdown timer with a resolution of 1 second.
Ex_watch.opl   Stopwatch with a resolution of 1 second.

